[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-38096"] :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070092/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-1)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -5 \\\\ 2 & -8\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809/selection/f1c2e730010a4821311f28beba209b5230f5d88e8dcf643d986bf10906a618a7" :answer/id #uuid "6e5ab615-3c39-57ba-a8a8-01ef20a332ad" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809/selection/bb4680c5f61219fcc620c3312074ae70b635b513e69ac6eae7c9e879817f1667" :answer/id #uuid "6e424319-ef94-5dfa-aff2-86acb84a4024" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809/selection/480a7a2906fa37e0de31965220147e6e6f85ff90d559eb7cee952b286ea1f32d" :answer/id #uuid "8ef43e3a-cda9-5020-acb4-21ce9d200d01" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}9 & 6 \\\\ -22 & -15\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809/selection/4d097fffec2a1514969402f4e1bd0d18e864df9b680c25392d623d0dc28a5284" :answer/id #uuid "bd3ac22a-01b8-5370-b0bc-d5302f7a8d03" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809/selection/5b44a83bcf37c07b375034f01d6be0de57be17d4010bd1c71488d33d6bf0afb5" :answer/id #uuid "0f1f3e4f-30fa-5a82-8dea-e5ef25816576" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "7ce533f6-294a-5e6a-aeaa-9556bcfe8b5e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-38809/selection/f1c2e730010a4821311f28beba209b5230f5d88e8dcf643d986bf10906a618a7" :answer-field/choices ["q-38809/selection/f1c2e730010a4821311f28beba209b5230f5d88e8dcf643d986bf10906a618a7" "q-38809/selection/bb4680c5f61219fcc620c3312074ae70b635b513e69ac6eae7c9e879817f1667" "q-38809/selection/480a7a2906fa37e0de31965220147e6e6f85ff90d559eb7cee952b286ea1f32d" "q-38809/selection/4d097fffec2a1514969402f4e1bd0d18e864df9b680c25392d623d0dc28a5284" "q-38809/selection/5b44a83bcf37c07b375034f01d6be0de57be17d4010bd1c71488d33d6bf0afb5"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-38809" :question/id #uuid "99a47024-381b-53ae-b4e4-9c86f82427cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-38809" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]},\\,C={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the bases $B$ and $C$ of ${R}^{2},$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$, shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070092/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1},\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nFirst, let's denote the vectors of $B$ and $C$ as ${{b}_{1},{b}_{2}}$ and ${{c}_{1},{c}_{2}}$, respectively.\n\nThe change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C$ is a matrix whose columns are the coordinates of vectors from $B$ relative to the basis $C.$\n\nHence, we need to find the coordinates of ${b}_{1}$ and ${b}_{2}$ relative to the basis $C.$ To do this, we consider the matrix\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | & | \\\\ {c}_{1} & {c}_{2} & {b}_{1} & {b}_{2} \\\\ | & | & | & |\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWe reduce $M$ using Gaussian elimination until we get the identity matrix on the left. By doing this, we obtain the required change-of-coordinates matrix on the right.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 8 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 & 3\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5-3\\cdot 2}[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-38809/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "86028fae-a119-5194-975d-a6d9fad6faf5"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-38809"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116/selection/5e34beed7b0211ab936a70b24c1c60b85752f768a5f533ab75a8d8f5888c964b" :answer/id #uuid "5631daa8-3a75-5ef0-bcc7-e2718a47416b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}12 & -5 \\\\ 26 & -11\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116/selection/39ab7bbc2d6ce69c19b47010952af1868d601289d13c1a3362c5538943949427" :answer/id #uuid "17ee376f-cfe4-5d01-8960-02079d97ffac" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116/selection/177eec5b896f91d54c45a69a20ad576ccdb0f0ada12d06b432e2fdb188db0dbd" :answer/id #uuid "f6f23802-5e26-5b73-bab2-1695814c7e29" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116/selection/b4e20e0f8f5cc03a397a1da58e4ebaa7f6338fc543029ef16f4a03993d93f872" :answer/id #uuid "06ea9253-4abb-5a4d-8a52-41f5687a093d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}10 & -7 \\\\ 24 & -17\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116/selection/7278f3c8ee765b6d143d5c2efb945cb20c7e22101b87e9b88215f53fb4783cf9" :answer/id #uuid "34aa0606-03f6-5125-9b72-d7ba219314fd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ -2 & -7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fe2a4d1-d2f3-5886-94a2-6f4af9e7ab64" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97116/selection/39ab7bbc2d6ce69c19b47010952af1868d601289d13c1a3362c5538943949427" :answer-field/choices ["q-97116/selection/5e34beed7b0211ab936a70b24c1c60b85752f768a5f533ab75a8d8f5888c964b" "q-97116/selection/39ab7bbc2d6ce69c19b47010952af1868d601289d13c1a3362c5538943949427" "q-97116/selection/177eec5b896f91d54c45a69a20ad576ccdb0f0ada12d06b432e2fdb188db0dbd" "q-97116/selection/b4e20e0f8f5cc03a397a1da58e4ebaa7f6338fc543029ef16f4a03993d93f872" "q-97116/selection/7278f3c8ee765b6d143d5c2efb945cb20c7e22101b87e9b88215f53fb4783cf9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97116" :question/id #uuid "4f59fe0b-284b-5212-bd9c-6b6ffbb22f39" :question/math-academy-id "q-97116" :question/problem "$$\n[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,{P}_{B\\to C}=[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to the basis $B$ and the change-of-coordinates matrix ${P}_{B\\to C}$ shown above. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the bases $B$ and $C$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070092/assets/1b81504d6fdcabee0e1f586fef3dd2af5a57a8411ba4d22429e00e09b171a4d1.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{C}={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1}\\,,\n$$\n\nwhere ${P}_{B\\to C}$ is the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $C.$\n\nOur goal is to compute $[T]_{C}.$ First, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to C}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 5-(-2)\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the basis $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{C} & ={P}_{B\\to C}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to C}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 9 \\\\ -2 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-97116/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61bd0b4f-165c-5f31-b4ec-e0eff7e758e1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97116"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120/selection/5907f35329e84b36f37943dbc80e51c0a3bc1cbcc61cfe56fb0883589cd6ebf4" :answer/id #uuid "29ffd46b-028c-582e-aa34-90a9fa6a81ed" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}11 & 7 \\\\ 8 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120/selection/f18fa2db27f7c241a1d2001d0b31a2a6cc8d45e1f781720031402733e603d5a6" :answer/id #uuid "4e9a7bea-9fb0-5ce8-921c-4d859382388d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120/selection/cb47858913b49e65309338697ce593bba0b8322237d62647252541a089a40715" :answer/id #uuid "bfc67d3b-2d8a-5d23-be68-058d2131bb66" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}17 & -2 \\\\ -3 & 4\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120/selection/9d1a0e4b2ef72b5ee3bf612ea2c4ba094c6d39d2ca5e1ec51c1897637b2a2856" :answer/id #uuid "1d8f4b24-e29c-59c9-ba1b-d029ed318afe" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120/selection/9a8a3f21196629df93df2035c250becff650efa7993732ab0503bae6544ed8ce" :answer/id #uuid "db64580f-ffed-5f64-a0bc-8c31942cfca9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-7 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5c93c890-81e9-5f10-821c-bf5dd5455496" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97120/selection/9d1a0e4b2ef72b5ee3bf612ea2c4ba094c6d39d2ca5e1ec51c1897637b2a2856" :answer-field/choices ["q-97120/selection/5907f35329e84b36f37943dbc80e51c0a3bc1cbcc61cfe56fb0883589cd6ebf4" "q-97120/selection/f18fa2db27f7c241a1d2001d0b31a2a6cc8d45e1f781720031402733e603d5a6" "q-97120/selection/cb47858913b49e65309338697ce593bba0b8322237d62647252541a089a40715" "q-97120/selection/9d1a0e4b2ef72b5ee3bf612ea2c4ba094c6d39d2ca5e1ec51c1897637b2a2856" "q-97120/selection/9a8a3f21196629df93df2035c250becff650efa7993732ab0503bae6544ed8ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97120" :question/id #uuid "521075a2-a304-5840-a75f-21a6502344fc" :question/math-academy-id "q-97120" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070092/assets/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\n \n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 6}[\\begin{aligned}5 & -6 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 9 \\\\ 1 & 7\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-5 & 6 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97120/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97120"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482/selection/aeb8b51f48eedcf34e948fa49a6cd37bcea3bc3ab9f32c98d08377228a1f4d12" :answer/id #uuid "88643928-a221-5d54-9574-72c2f8cd9f7d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -1 \\\\ 9 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482/selection/a67ebac95df9108d5d26a01ad2ac475a083c0fc37e5b62cb90e3c2cc6047d000" :answer/id #uuid "0ac9e8ea-746e-5628-8717-3115f17fe124" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 39 \\\\ 8 & -5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482/selection/06bc6a5d424c08cecbd75279d9447d743e9ab08b3d54831e2c425e23fba04b60" :answer/id #uuid "51d599af-36d8-560c-940b-0d2c5e18e818" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 5 \\\\ 39 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482/selection/1c6c96b356bd1805a32a31af2d10d72ad8b0706eb417e702135e2ebd0a9aeefb" :answer/id #uuid "baee1d1b-d00c-5acb-94f6-f0427a62b462" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-39 & 8 \\\\ 5 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482/selection/54d03d815bb8066629459377b1a97f765a995655232bbd6dcafaa040c499c7ab" :answer/id #uuid "ac6e1902-07ed-50fd-88a1-9411422c1346" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "21999da2-cdb2-5afa-a867-f7b96c23e2f1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-140482/selection/54d03d815bb8066629459377b1a97f765a995655232bbd6dcafaa040c499c7ab" :answer-field/choices ["q-140482/selection/aeb8b51f48eedcf34e948fa49a6cd37bcea3bc3ab9f32c98d08377228a1f4d12" "q-140482/selection/a67ebac95df9108d5d26a01ad2ac475a083c0fc37e5b62cb90e3c2cc6047d000" "q-140482/selection/06bc6a5d424c08cecbd75279d9447d743e9ab08b3d54831e2c425e23fba04b60" "q-140482/selection/1c6c96b356bd1805a32a31af2d10d72ad8b0706eb417e702135e2ebd0a9aeefb" "q-140482/selection/54d03d815bb8066629459377b1a97f765a995655232bbd6dcafaa040c499c7ab"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-140482" :question/id #uuid "81e8f58d-3db1-5493-9653-beb052e8ad62" :question/math-academy-id "q-140482" :question/problem "$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]},\\,[T]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nConsider the basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the matrix $[T]_{B}$ of a linear transformation $T$ with respect to this basis. Find the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S.$" :question/worked-solution "The connection between the matrices of our linear transformation $T$ relative to the basis $B$ and standard basis $S$ is given by the following diagram:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14070092/assets/dbd020362f950fe8bfb4c592652b9e78a73610fa01a247b0b7ead6f201bf9ea5.png)\n\nHere, moving along an arrow means pre-multiplying by the corresponding matrix. Algebraically, we can write this as\n\n$$\n[T]_{S}={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1},\n$$\n\nand the change-of-coordinates matrix from $B$ to $S$ is\n\n$$\n{P}_{B\\to S}=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the inverse of ${P}_{B\\to S}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} & ={[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot (-1)-(-1)\\cdot 5}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can compute the matrix of $T$ relative to the standard basis $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[T]_{S} & ={P}_{B\\to S}\\cdot [T]_{B}\\cdot {P}_{B\\to S}^{-1} \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}7 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-1 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & -39 \\\\ 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-140482/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "969220db-a686-511b-b33a-0b4f6ab66b1a"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-140482"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
